================================================================================
## Ontology Evolve: Stage 0 fixture, eval dataset and baseline runner
================================================================================

Context: Ontology → Evolve turns a business question the ontology cannot
answer into a reviewed relationship or mapping fix. Before any feature code,
the AI-feature lifecycle (rule 12) needs a committed dataset and a baseline
harness, and the evaluation needs fixture data whose answers are known
independently of the ontology.

Changes:

1. tests/fixtures/evolution/supply_chain.sql
   Supply-chain fixture (orders, order lines, products, suppliers) with
   declared PK/FK constraints, negative variants (no FK, orphan key,
   duplicate product id, ambiguous supplier name, restricted table) and a
   hand-authored gold_answers table.
2. tests/fixtures/evolution/gold_check.sql
   Recomputes every gold answer with plain SQL; all must match.
3. tests/fixtures/evolution/seed_supply_chain.py
   Seeds the fixture through the Databricks CLI, checks gold, prints Delta
   table versions.
4. tests/fixtures/evolution/supply_chain_domain.json
   Fixture domain: Order, OrderLine, Product, Supplier; hasLine and
   suppliedBy mapped; no OrderLine → Product relationship.
5. tests/eval/datasets/agent_ontology_evolution/baseline.jsonl
   30 rows (20 dev, 10 holdout) covering supported, missing relationship,
   broken mapping, ambiguous term/path, identity, access, missing source,
   unsupported form, unknown concept, stale, cancel/retry and adversarial.
6. tests/eval/judges/ontology_evolution.py
   Rule-based judges (contract, readiness, states, gap, ops, decision,
   abstention, false-ready, execution-based gold).
7. tests/eval/run_agent_ontology_evolution.py
   Runner; dry run validates the dataset contract.
8. tests/eval/thresholds.yaml
   ontology_evolution thresholds.

Files modified:
- tests/fixtures/evolution/supply_chain.sql
- tests/fixtures/evolution/gold_check.sql
- tests/fixtures/evolution/seed_supply_chain.py
- tests/fixtures/evolution/supply_chain_domain.json
- tests/eval/datasets/agent_ontology_evolution/baseline.jsonl
- tests/eval/judges/ontology_evolution.py
- tests/eval/run_agent_ontology_evolution.py
- tests/eval/thresholds.yaml

Tests:
- Baseline before changes: `uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"` —
  11090 passed, 335 skipped.
- `uv run --frozen python tests/eval/run_agent_ontology_evolution.py` —
  schema_valid=1.000, n=30, holdout=10.
- Live seed on fe-vm-lakebase-praneeth: gold_check 9/9 match.

================================================================================
## Ontology Evolve: Stage 1 run state, persistence, flag and router
================================================================================

Context: Evolve keeps each candidate as run-owned state until a builder
accepts it, because a candidate written as the next domain version would
become the default target of the external API, MCP, scheduler and GitHub
mirror (they resolve the numeric-latest version of any status). Run state
therefore lives in its own Lakebase tables with revision-checked updates.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/EvolutionRuns.py
   New mixin: evolution_runs (mutable, revision CAS, idempotency key unique
   per domain) and evolution_results (append-only). Portable SQL only
   (ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING RETURNING; UPDATE … WHERE revision = %s); writes
   raise instead of being dropped.
2. src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/{store.py,__init__.py,schema.sql}
   Wire the mixin, ready flag, known tables and DDL.
3. src/back/objects/registry/store/base.py
   Evolution methods raise InfrastructureError on stores without support.
4. scripts/bootstrap/lakebase-perms.sh, scripts/_internal/_lakebase_preflight.py
   Owner bootstrap DDL and preflight expectations for the new tables.
5. src/back/objects/ontology/evolution/
   RunStatus, CoverageState, Decision, Intent, IntentFilter, content_hash,
   EvolutionService (explicit parent version + content hash, idempotent
   create, CAS update, intent edit invalidates derived results, cancel,
   interrupted recovery, stale-parent check).
6. src/api/routers/internal/evolution.py, internal/__init__.py,
   shared/fastapi/main.py
   /evolution router (capabilities, runs CRUD, intent, cancel); folder must
   match the loaded context (409 otherwise); builder-only writes;
   domain-scoped, not status-gated.
7. src/shared/config/settings.py, app.yaml.template
   ONTOBRICKS_EVOLUTION_ENABLED, default false.

Files modified:
- src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/EvolutionRuns.py (new)
